//! blyg-render: the studio preview pipeline (Markdown → HTML exactly as a blyg publishes it).
//!
//! A Rust port of the reference Worker's studio preview: markdown-it with
//! `html: false` + linkify + the embeds extension, TK scopes stripped and
//! tinted, and (threads only) `![[id]]` quotes resolved from the local store
//! and baked as `blockquote.blyg-transclusion` with a provenance line, and
//! (both kinds) `[[id]]` links resolved to anchors.
//! Parity with the Worker is tested against fixtures generated by running
//! the Worker's own TypeScript (see `tests/fixtures/gen_parity.mjs` and
//! `docs/RENDER.md`).
//!
//! ```
//! use blyg_render::{render_preview, Kind, NoResolver, RenderOpts};
//! let out = render_preview("Hello *world*", Kind::Fragment, &NoResolver, &RenderOpts::default());
//! assert_eq!(out.html, "<p data-line=\"0\">Hello <em>world</em></p>\n");
//! ```

